+# R48b — MMVQ A-side hoist (lane-235, kernel-maker draft)
+
+Inherited: `9ff4644b1dee75c3d1040c91ae306eb8388e65c0` — *feat(updater): preserve fork work across
+rebases* — on branch `lane-235/r48b-mmvq-a-hoist-2026-09-14` in worktree
+`C:/ArifiLabs/cache/r48b-mmvq-wt`. No commit made, no branch moved.
+
+**Status of §1-§9: the original DRAFT, NOT BUILT text, kept verbatim as the record. See §10 for what
+has since been rebuilt, compiled and run.** As written below: a measurement chain owned the box,
+nothing here was compiled, no shader was generated, no test was run. Every claim in §1-§9 is either a
+source reading (CHECKED, with file:line) or a stated assumption for HQ's build and pairing to
+resolve. §10 supersedes that status and says exactly what has since been compiled and run.
+
+---
+
+## 1. Mechanism
+
+CHECKED, `ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/vulkan-shaders/mul_mat_vecq.comp:36-78` at the inherited SHA:
+
+```
+iter():  for j in NUM_COLS { load B block; for n in num_rows { mmvq_dot_product(a_idx, b_qs_idx) } }
+```
+
+`mmvq_dot_product()` performs the **entire A-side decode** — `repack4()` +
+`get_dm_scale()` / `get_d_scale()` / `get_scale()` / `sx8_range()` + `sx8_levels4()`, depending on
+the type arm — before it touches a single B word (`mul_mat_vecq_funcs.glsl:370-435` for Q4_K/Q5_K,
+and the same shape in all nine other arms). Its two arguments are `a_block_idx` and `b_qs_idx`:
+
+- `a_block_idx = (first_row*p.ncols + n*p.ncols + col)/QUANT_K_Q8_1 + a_offset` — depends on
+  `n` and `col` only.
+- `b_qs_idx = tid % (32 / K_PER_ITER)` — loop-invariant for the whole dispatch.
+
+**Neither depends on `j`.** So the weight decode is repeated NUM_COLS times per (row, k-slice), a
+NUM_COLS-fold redundancy on every MMVQ type. That is the candidate mechanism for the per-width step
+lane-198 measured (q4_K 1.9-2.3x per dispatch at width 4->5) and for the NUM_COLS==7 tail noted at
+`ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/ggml-vulkan.cpp:11740-11755`.
+
+### The change
+
+Every type arm is split into two functions that between them are the old body, in the old order:
+
+| function | contains | depends on |
+|---|---|---|
+| `mmvq_load_a(ib_a, iqs) -> mmvq_a_t` | the whole A decode | A only |
+| `mmvq_dot_a(a) -> FLOAT_TYPE` | the integer dots against `cache_b_qs` + the scale apply | A state + cached B |
+| `mmvq_dot_product(ib_a, iqs)` | `mmvq_dot_a(mmvq_load_a(ib_a, iqs))` | unchanged entry point |
+
+`iter()` then has two nests behind one specialization constant:
+
+- **OFF** (`ARIFI_MMVQ_A_HOIST == 0`, or `NUM_COLS == 1`): upstream's nest verbatim, calling
+  `mmvq_dot_product()`.
+- **ON**: decode A once per (row, k-slice) into `mmvq_a_t a_dec[NUM_ROWS]`, then loop `j` doing only
+  the B load and `mmvq_dot_a(a_dec[n])`.
+
+Bit-identity is **by construction, not by inspection**: both paths call the same
+`mmvq_load_a`/`mmvq_dot_a` pair, the arithmetic expressions are byte-for-byte the ones that shipped,
+and the accumulation order inside each call is unchanged. Nothing is reassociated; the float adds
+into `temp[j][n]` happen in the same order in both nests.
+
+### Runtime switch
+
+`layout (constant_id = 3) const uint ARIFI_MMVQ_A_HOIST = 0;` (mul_mat_vecq.comp:47).
+
+**Default 0 in the shader on purpose.** The host supplies the value per pipeline; any create site
+that omits the constant keeps upstream's nest rather than silently opting in. (The q6_k
+direct-scales constant defaults to 1 — copying that here would have turned the hoist on for every
+vendor through any site I missed.)
+
+Host (`ggml-vulkan.cpp:7054-7092`):
+
+| knob | effect |
+|---|---|
+| device probe | ON for `VK_VENDOR_ID_AMD`, OFF for every other vendor |
+| `GGML_ARIFI_MMVQ_A_HOIST=0\|1` | overrides the probe in both directions, same binary |
+| `GGML_ARIFI_MMVQ_A_HOIST_IQ1=1` | additionally turns it on for IQ1_S and IQ1_M (default OFF, see §3); never above the global switch |
+| `NUM_COLS == 1` | folds to OFF at pipeline-compile time — no redundancy exists at one column |
+
+Receipt at device init, on stderr, the same channel as the q6_k line and for the same reason
+(llama-server drops ggml INFO):
+
+```
+ggml_vulkan: mmvq A-side hoist: ON (device-probe) (iq1: OFF)
+ggml_vulkan: mmvq A-side hoist: OFF (GGML_ARIFI_MMVQ_A_HOIST) (iq1: OFF)
+```
+
+The source field is not decoration: a pairing log has to prove *probe* against *override*, not just
+ON against OFF. Same standard as the `RDNA3 mul_mat_vec_id rows = %u (%s)` receipt (win #24).
+
