+## 3. Register estimate
+
+A-side live state, in 32-bit registers **per row**, read off the struct each arm now declares. It is
+a function of NUM_ROWS only — independent of NUM_COLS, which is the point of the change.
+
+| type | struct | regs/row | rows at NUM_COLS 2-4 | rows at NUM_COLS 5-8 | worst A state | default |
+|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
+| Q8_0, Q4_0, Q5_0, MXFP4, ROCMFP4_FAST | `i32vec2 + float` | 3 | 1 (2 for mxfp4/fp4) | 4 | 12 | ON |
+| Q4_1, Q5_1 | `i32vec2 + vec2` | 4 | 1 | 4 | 16 | ON |
+| Q2_0, Q2_0_G128 | `i32vec4 + float` | 5 | 2 | 4 | 20 | ON |
+| Q3_K, Q6_K | `i32vec4 + float` | 5 | 1 | 4 | 20 | ON |
+| Q4_K, Q5_K | `i32vec4 + vec2` | 6 | 1 | 4 | 24 | ON |
+| Q2_K | `i32vec4 + vec2 + scale + scale_m` | 8 | 2 | 4 | 32 | ON |
+| S-X8 | `int32 lv[8] + float rlo[4] + float step[4]` | **16** | 2 (`sx8_num_rows`) | 2 | 32 | ON |
+| IQ1_S | `2x i32vec4 + vec2` | 10 | 4 | 4 | 40 | **OFF** |
+| IQ1_M | `int32 grid[4] + float dl[4] + float delta[4]` | **12** | 4 | 4 | 48 | **OFF** |
+
+Row counts are CHECKED for this box (AMD RDNA3, non-GCN): `rm_stdq_int = 1`, `rm_kq_int = 1`,
+`rm_iq_int(i) = 8 at i==0 else 4`, `rm_int_n(rows, i) = 4 when i >= 4`, `sx8_num_rows = 2` by
+default (`ggml-vulkan.cpp:6859-6862, 6993, 7203`).
+
+Notes that matter:
+
+- **NUM_COLS == 1 is free.** That is the width with the most rows per workgroup (`rm_iq_int(0) = 8`),
+  and it is exactly the width where the hoist folds OFF. The 8-row IQ1 case never pays A-state
+  registers.
+- **`temp[NUM_COLS][NUM_ROWS]` is unchanged** and is the other live set: up to 8 x 4 = 32 registers at
+  the wide end, the same in both arms.
+- **S-X8 is the one to watch.** 16 regs/row is the heaviest per-row state, and it is an acceptance
+  target, so it is NOT gated off. At the default `sx8_num_rows = 2` that is 32 registers. If the ON
+  arm regresses on S-X8, `GGML_VK_SX8_MMV_ROWS=1` halves it with no rebuild
+  (`ggml-vulkan.cpp:5702`) — pair that before concluding the hoist is wrong for the type. The
+  fallback inside the type, if rows=1 is not enough, is to hoist only the 8 level words and
+  recompute `sx8_range()` per column (16 -> 8 regs/row); I did not pick that blind.
+- **IQ1_S / IQ1_M ship OFF** on register grounds alone — 10 and 12 regs/row at 4 rows, the highest
+  product in the table. The gate is in the HOST (a different specialization value for those two
+  pipelines), not an `#ifdef`: the shader carries both paths, so
+  `GGML_ARIFI_MMVQ_A_HOIST_IQ1=1` moves them for a pairing with no rebuild. Runtime-switch law
+  satisfied.
+
+**Primary uncertainty, stated as such:** `mmvq_a_t a_dec[NUM_ROWS]` must be scalarized into
+registers, not spilled to scratch. I structured both loops as static trips over the specialization
+constant `NUM_ROWS` with an `if (n < num_rows)` guard rather than a runtime trip count over
+`num_rows`, precisely so the array has a compile-time-known extent and every index is a constant
+after unrolling. That part — constant-indexed array-of-struct — is the SROA-friendly half.
+
+The **named suspect** is the other half: `mmvq_dot_a(const mmvq_a_t a)` takes the struct **by
+value**, and glslang does not inline. It emits a real `OpFunctionCall` with a Function-storage
+`OpVariable` for the parameter and a whole-struct `OpStore` into it, sourced from an `OpAccessChain`
+into `a_dec[]`. For IQ1_M (12 dwords) and S-X8 (16) that per-call copy is the specific pattern most
+likely to land in scratch and eat the entire win. Both of those are already the heaviest rows of the
+table, so a uniform slowdown concentrated on exactly those two types is the signature.
+
+**The repair I did NOT take, named so it is not re-derived from scratch:** drop the array-of-struct
+for per-field arrays (`int32_t lv[8][NUM_ROWS]`, `float rlo[4][NUM_ROWS]`, …) held as locals in
+`iter()` and pass nothing — which removes the by-value struct parameter entirely. It costs the clean
+`mmvq_load_a`/`mmvq_dot_a` symmetry and therefore the free bit-identity argument, so it is not worth
+taking blind. Take it only if arm B is uniformly slower and the disassembly shows the parameter copy.
+`GGML_VULKAN_PERF` timings plus an RGA/`spirv-dis` look at the SPIR-V is the discriminator here —
+not another source read.
+
