+## 6. Planted reds
+
+Two, because they answer different questions. HQ applies one at a time, confirms RED, reverts.
+
+### RED-1 — proves the decode site is live (fires on BOTH arms)
+
+Because ON and OFF share `mmvq_load_a()`, an error planted inside it must turn both arms red. That
+is the intended reading: it proves the decode site executes on every path, and it is the check that
+the shared-function refactor did not orphan an arm. Per type, in
+`ggml/src/ggml-vulkan/vulkan-shaders/mul_mat_vecq_funcs.glsl`, inside that type's `mmvq_load_a`:
+
+```diff
+ mmvq_a_t mmvq_load_a(const uint ib_a, const uint iqs) {
+     mmvq_a_t a;
+     a.qs       = repack4(ib_a, iqs * 4);
+     a.dm_scale = get_dm_scale(ib_a, iqs * 4);
++    a.qs.x ^= 0x88888888;   // R48b RED-1 (Q4_K/Q5_K decode site)
+     return a;
+ }
+```
+
+**The constant is `0x88888888`, NOT `0x00000001` — corrected 2026-09-14.** The weak plant is not
+reliably red and must not be used. `^ 0x00000001` flips the low bit of ONE nibble in one of the four
+packed words: for Q4_K that is a single weight out of the 16 this call consumes, moved by 1 level out
+of 15. The resulting relative RMS error is order 1e-2 and the NMSE order 1e-4 — the same order as
+test-backend-ops' own MUL_MAT NMSE tolerance, so a run can come back GREEN with the plant in place
+and HQ would read that as "the decode site is dead" when it is not. A red that can pass is worse than
+no red.
+
+`^ 0x88888888` flips the top bit of **every** nibble in that word. The repacked quants are
+`0x0F0F0F0F`- or `0x03030303`-masked, so each affected byte becomes `0x8X` — a large NEGATIVE value
+under the signed `dotPacked4x8EXT`, not a small perturbation. Four weights out of 16 go wrong by
+roughly a full dynamic range, NMSE order 1e-1, two-to-three orders above tolerance. The same argument
+holds for the two array plants: `a.grid[0] ^= 0x88888888` reddens both the `>> 0` and the `>> 4`
+extraction in IQ1_M's `l == 0`, and `a.lv[0] ^= 0x88888888` drives S-X8 levels (range 0..63,
+so bit 7 clear in every byte) negative.
+
+Replace the constant in every row of the table below; the field names and the insertion point are
+unchanged.
+
+One decode site per type arm. The file has ten `#if` blocks; this is the map from type to the
+exact line, so all ten are applicable without guessing. In each case the line goes **immediately
+before the `return a;`** of that arm's `mmvq_load_a`.
+
